{"kind":"request","text":"The next creation cohort: a failed claim frees its place\n\nScope: from 61243b79 and the decisions 9af818a5, cccd205a and 908b6d86. Build one next cohort that new rooms can take as the default.\n\nThe scene: a host goes down for an hour. People keep running `dap create` on a register, and each claim's three attempts fail. When the host returns, the operator reads the register's log. Each failed claim has a final failed state, its place in `max` is free again, and new rooms start. A person who ran `dap create` during the outage can tell that their claim failed and that a new one is safe.\n\nCarry in this cohort:\n1. Option A of 61243b79: a final failed state, set when the last attempt closes with nothing selected, with a late confirmed reply going to `delete-repository`. This is the reason for the cohort.\n2. `separate-recovery`: refuse a founder key that is also the recovery key.\n3. The one-hour read token of the note at 970c701c, with no `hours` field. Real call 2 clears it for clones that have started. State what the note says about a token that ends between two requests of one clone, and that no clone has run past a one-hour token.\n\nDo not carry `revoke-reads` or the founder retirement. They join later if a slice needs them.\n\nTo be the default, this cohort must close the limits that 991129fc names: checker-key invitations, journal archive export, the page's offer and `apps/views`, and a replay of a journal from the new pins' bytes. Name any limit you think should stay, with the reason. I decide those in the review.\n\nDone when a new register on this cohort survives the scene above in a test with scripted failures, a scratch room on a deployed Worker runs on it through the real commands, `dap install` and the page's offer use it by default, and existing rooms keep their pins. I change the Workers' creation pins in that head's deploy record. Say what an existing register does: it stays as it is, and the docs state the way out.\n\nOrder: after J2 and J5.","body":{"conditions":"A new default creation cohort carries a failed claim's final state, separate-recovery and the one-hour read token, survives scripted host failures, runs a scratch room on a deployed Worker, approved by the checker and landed on main.","target_head":"d2e6c82cc07ff296da2d72946ab61707780e872b","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}